From 2471e7d4f4a59f43849ce84681ca1eaedfacd0bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 10:43:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] framework/logstore: include tenant_id in list select
 columns

The Stage 4 logs migration added the tenant_id column and the logging
plugin stamps it correctly on every tenant-routed /v1 call, but the
list query's column allow-list (listSelectColumns) never selected the
column back.  /api/logs responses then returned tenant_id=null for
every row even when the row's value was populated, and the
dashboard's per-tenant filter (?tenant_id=current) returned an empty
result set against rows it actually contained matches for.

Drop tenant_id into the select clause alongside the other scope
columns (user_id / team_id / customer_id / business_unit_id) so the
list response carries the value the JSON tag expects.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
---
 framework/logstore/rdb.go | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/framework/logstore/rdb.go b/framework/logstore/rdb.go
index 77a0dfdd8..329c178e7 100644
--- a/framework/logstore/rdb.go
+++ b/framework/logstore/rdb.go
@@ -769,6 +769,10 @@ func (s *RDBLogStore) listSelectColumns() string {
 		"routing_engines_used", "routing_rule_id", "routing_rule_name",
 		"user_id", "team_id", "team_name", "customer_id", "customer_name",
 		"business_unit_id", "business_unit_name",
+		// tenant_id (Stage 4 multi-tenant): without this, the dashboard's
+		// per-tenant filter strips every row even when the column is
+		// populated, because list responses come back with tenant_id=null.
+		"tenant_id",
 		"speech_input", "transcription_input", "image_generation_input", "video_generation_input",
 		"latency", "token_usage", "cost", "status", "error_details", "stream",
 		"content_summary", "metadata", "cache_debug",
